      "locator": "::node-45",
      "line": 42,
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [],
      "source_text": "No previous probability course is needed. Start with events and finite probability tables, then conditioning and transitions. Gaussian formulas use the matrix review in Primer A; the probability language is introduced here. Treat the measure-theory background and longer proofs as a second pass after you can do the Easy and Medium problems.",
